# The 2022 decoder of the tutorial "Old against new at the same serving cost", built as
# OPT, GPT-NeoX and Pythia were: multi-head attention with RoPE at base 10k on every
# channel, a LayerNorm before each branch, a GELU MLP four times the width, biases and
# an untied head. One number sizes it, the width: a layer for each 128 of it, and a
# head of 128 for each 128, so that d_model = 4096 is OPT-6.7B's shape, 32 layers of
# 32 heads, 6.4B parameters besides the embeddings.
use agentic_code

d_model    = 4096
vocab_size = 50304                       # GPT-NeoX's 50277 tokens, padded

norm  = layernorm(eps=1e-5, bias=true)
attn  = gqa(num_heads=d_model // 128, num_kv_heads=d_model // 128, bias=true,
            rope=rope(base=10000))
ffn   = mlp(intermediate_size=4 * d_model, activation=gelu, bias=true)
block = [norm attn] [norm ffn]

layers = d_model // 128
model  = embed block^layers norm head

# The target as it would train: 20 tokens for each of its 6.44B parameters besides the
# embeddings, a batch by DeepSeek LLM's law (3.7M tokens), the learning rate the 2022
# ladder's searches found, its parameters and AdamW's split over a node by FSDP.
# old_ladder.bux sizes it down and sets each of these for its rungs.
budget       = 129B
batch        = 1792
optimizer.lr = 1.5e-3
mesh         = mesh(fsdp=8)
